OL,3,GNEWSARail disaster of 1957 marked by St
OL,4,AJohn's plaque
OL,5,
OL,6,FA memorial plaque at St John's station
OL,7,Fin south-east London is to mark the
OL,8,Fdeaths of 90 people in one of the worst
OL,9,Fdisasters in British railway history.
OL,11,FMany more were also injured in the
OL,12,Fcrash on 4 December 1957.
OL,14,FThis is the first memorial in St John's
OL,15,Fto honour those who were caught up in
OL,16,Fthe accident, in which two crowded
OL,17,Ftrains - one electric, one steam -
OL,18,Fcrashed on a foggy winter's evening.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
